    "body": "### Contact Details (e.g. Tox ID or email)\n\n_No response_\n\n### qTox Version\n\nv1.18.4-6-gaeef7e241\n\n### Commit Hash\n\naeef7e241c4c994661c32109f78c9458771f425a\n\n### Toxcore Version\n\n0.2.22\n\n### Qt Version\n\n6.8.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Start qTox;\n2. Сlick on \"My Profile\";\n3. Сlick on the link `Current profile location: C:/Users/Max/AppData/Roaming/tox`\n\n### Observed Behavior\n\nNothing happens Windows Explorer won't open.\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nWindows Explorer or another file manager opens\n\n### Reproducibility\n\nAlways\n\n### Operating System\n\nWindows\n\n### Operating System version/distro/name/etc.\n\nWindows 11\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\n[15:18:16.414 UTC] (default) /src/qtbase/src/plugins/platforms/windows/qwindowsservices.cpp:115 : Warning: ShellExecute 'file://c/Users/Max/AppData/Roaming/tox' failed (error 5).\n```",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Apparently the problem is in Qt which converts the path to msys2 format (cygpath). Because judging by the code, the visible path string is supplied with the `file://` prefix.  And at the output in the logs we see another line",
